/-!
# Mask geometry for low-rank matrix completion (`supp.tex`, Lemma `lem:mask_geometry`)

Setting of the source: `M₀ ∈ ℝ^{m×n}` has rank `r` and a compact SVD `M₀ = U₀ Σ₀ V₀ᵀ`,
`Ω` is a Bernoulli(`p`) observation mask, `P_Ω` keeps observed entries and zeroes the rest,
`J` is the all-ones matrix and `Id` the identity operator on the ambient matrix space.  The
target objects are

* `W_Ω  = p⁻¹ Ω − J`                     (`Wmask`),
* `T_Ω  = p⁻¹ P_Ω − Id`, acting as the Schur product `A ↦ W_Ω ⊙ A` (`Tmask`),
* `T_⋆  = {U₀ Aᵀ + B V₀ᵀ : A ∈ ℝ^{n×r}, B ∈ ℝ^{m×r}}` (`MemTangentRect`),
* `b(A,C) = min{‖A‖_F ‖C‖_{2,∞}, ‖A‖_{2,∞} ‖C‖_F}` (`bFactor`).

Norms: `‖·‖` is the spectral (operator) norm (`specNorm`), `‖·‖_F` the unnormalized Frobenius
norm (`frobNorm`), `‖·‖_{2,∞}` the largest `L₂` norm of the rows (`rowNorm`), and `⟨·,·⟩` the
unnormalized Frobenius / Hilbert–Schmidt pairing (`frobInner`).  The probability statement is
over the observation mask only.
-/

